AI Context-Buyer Platform \emdash Google Ads API Design Overview\par
\par
1. Product name\par
AI Context-Buyer Platform \emdash multi-tenant SaaS for contextologists and agencies managing Google Ads (and Yandex Direct) for multiple client projects.\par
\par
2. Audience\par
B2B: advertising agencies and freelance performance marketers. Not a consumer app.\par
\par
3. Business model\par
SaaS workspace per organization. Each client is an isolated project with its own OAuth credentials, briefs, semantics, creatives, campaigns, and reports (project_id isolation).\par
\par
4. What the tool does with Google Ads API\par
- Connect a Google Ads account via OAuth 2.0 (scope: adwords).\par
- Build campaign drafts from brief / semantic / creatives pipeline.\par
- Create Search campaigns through the Google Ads API in PAUSED status.\par
- Publish only after explicit user confirmation in the UI (no unattended publish).\par
- Sync campaign list and pull performance reporting.\par
- Suggest optimizations; apply changes only with user confirmation.\par
- Keyword planning support via keyword ideas / related research steps.\par
\par
5. Architecture (high level)\par
User (Web UI) -> AI Context-Buyer API -> Connector Layer -> Google Ads API.\par
Business logic never calls Google SDK directly; only AdPlatformConnector.\par
OAuth access/refresh tokens are encrypted at rest per project.\par
\par
6. Campaign types currently supported\par
Search.\par
\par
7. Google Ads capabilities used\par
Campaign Creation, Campaign Management, Reporting, Keyword Planning Services.\par
\par
8. Security and policy alignment\par
- Per-project credential isolation.\par
- Encrypted token storage.\par
- No automatic campaign go-live without UI confirmation.\par
- Operator audit logging without storing raw secrets in logs.\par
